  If bias shrinks toward 0 as N grows (roughly monotonically, well below the std at each N), this is ordinary, expected shot noise with no hidden ratio-estimator bias floor. If bias stays roughly CONSTANT (does not shrink) even at N=1,000,000, that would indicate a real, hidden systematic problem -- worth flagging explicitly either way.
